            {
              "category": "external-boundary-assumptions",
              "file": "libs/infrastructure/src/review_v2/review_fix_runner/launch_context.rs",
              "line": 789,
              "message": "The polling loop treats any `/bin/kill -0 <pid>` failure as proof that the intended descendant vanished. Because only the numeric PID is recorded, PID reuse can make an unrelated process appear to be the descendant and cause a false timeout/failure during the five-second wait. Capture and compare a process identity (for example Linux `/proc/<pid>/stat` start time) or use an equivalent identity-safe mechanism before accepting the result.",
              "severity": "P2"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:d7f0f090addffd564fd00b2495b6fb32a4349728877bb7d5c97cd48afe142484",
          "type": "fast",
